From 93afd6121329d2c2508d42e0809e2268ea621bd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 06:37:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] system: keep the line of a disk that cannot be told apart

Two disks of one start with one model and serial number cannot be told apart:
internal-disk-choice keeps both away while a list exists, and neither is
offered. A line of the list for that key was lost when the list was saved
again, and with it what was chosen for the disk once it can be told apart.
Such a line ("twin" in "list") is now kept as the list has it. The texts that
name the disks that cannot be told apart say this case too.
---
 resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po | 4 ++--
 resources/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po | 8 ++++----
 resources/language/resource.language.es_es/strings.po | 8 ++++----
 resources/language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po | 8 ++++----
 resources/lib/modules/system.py                       | 9 ++++++++-
 5 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po b/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
index 9d76e0d..7a5b1ad 100644
--- a/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
+++ b/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
@@ -1545,7 +1545,7 @@ msgid "The internal disks are shown as chosen from the next start"
 msgstr ""
 
 msgctxt "#33151"
-msgid "These disks cannot be told apart from others (the kernel finds no serial number on them), so while any disk is kept away, they are kept away too: %s"
+msgid "These disks cannot be told apart from others (the kernel finds no serial number on them, or the same one on two disks), so while any disk is kept away, they are kept away too: %s"
 msgstr ""
 
 msgctxt "#33152"
@@ -1569,7 +1569,7 @@ msgid "Every internal disk is shown from the next start"
 msgstr ""
 
 msgctxt "#33157"
-msgid "With disks kept away, from the next start:[CR][CR]- Before anything else runs, this system lets go of the disks that are not ticked. Kodi, its add-ons and file sharing do not see them, and neither can a program that runs here with full rights reach them.[CR][CR]- The kernel attaches no other internal disk until the next start: a disk that is plugged in while the system runs is seen from the next start.[CR][CR]- The kernel runs with its lockdown, as in the normal start: it loads only the drivers that came with this system, not the ones that add-ons bring, and keeps programs away from the memory and the hardware of the computer.[CR][CR]- A disk with no serial number cannot be told apart from others, so it is kept away too, and every disk is kept away when the list cannot be read. The disk this system is on is never kept away.[CR][CR]- Where a disk that is to be kept away cannot be (the system cannot let go of it, or cannot tell which disk it starts from), it stays, and no partition of an internal disk is mounted in that start. That is said when Kodi starts.[CR][CR]- It holds against what runs in this system, until the next start. It does not hold against a program that changes this list or the boot menu and waits for the next start.[CR][CR]- It is so on every computer that this drive is started on: their disks go with the first line of the list."
+msgid "With disks kept away, from the next start:[CR][CR]- Before anything else runs, this system lets go of the disks that are not ticked. Kodi, its add-ons and file sharing do not see them, and neither can a program that runs here with full rights reach them.[CR][CR]- The kernel attaches no other internal disk until the next start: a disk that is plugged in while the system runs is seen from the next start.[CR][CR]- The kernel runs with its lockdown, as in the normal start: it loads only the drivers that came with this system, not the ones that add-ons bring, and keeps programs away from the memory and the hardware of the computer.[CR][CR]- A disk with no serial number, or with the same one as another disk, cannot be told apart from others, so it is kept away too, and every disk is kept away when the list cannot be read. The disk this system is on is never kept away.[CR][CR]- Where a disk that is to be kept away cannot be (the system cannot let go of it, or cannot tell which disk it starts from), it stays, and no partition of an internal disk is mounted in that start. That is said when Kodi starts.[CR][CR]- It holds against what runs in this system, until the next start. It does not hold against a program that changes this list or the boot menu and waits for the next start.[CR][CR]- It is so on every computer that this drive is started on: their disks go with the first line of the list."
 msgstr ""
 
 msgctxt "#33158"
